  "body": "Fork synced at v0.18.0. Not stacked (branched from upstream main at 3e9b8ae1).\n\n**What reproduced.** #1036 suspected the milled Bore ride plunges a cutter that is not centre-cutting into an undrilled hole unjudged. It does not. On a solid 60 x 60 x 20 block, a 20 mm hole and an 8 mm end mill marked `center_cutting: false`, the Bore arm generates a path whose every rung is entered by a zig-zag ramp along the radial sweep, with the note \"entry: the tool is not centre-cutting and may not plunge into solid (the plunge arm) - ramp along the first cut instead\"; the ring's re-entry plunges land on columns the sweep already cut. A 9 mm hole (no helix, no ramp run) is refused: \"entry refused: the tool is not centre-cutting - the plunge arm, and no helix or ramp fits onto Z 15.000\". The law doing it: `operation::generate` lays the tool's `center_cutting` over the generation's links (M11.3 B-D, 874507a8) and every planar-ladder descent asks it (`descent::plan_core`, `plunge_law::guard`, 515525c4). The Bore ride is a planar ladder.\n\n**What changed.** Tests only: `crates/app/tests/bore_entry.rs` pins the law on the Bore ride, and `docs/decisions/1036-bore-entry.md` records why no #992-style prior-stock refusal is added (an end mill without centre teeth may ramp or helix in; a thread mill cannot).\n\n**How tested.** Pinning tests (all pass):\n- `a_cutter_that_is_not_centre_cutting_ramps_into_an_undrilled_bore_never_plunges` - `plunge_law::first_solid_plunge` finds no axial plunge into solid; the ramp substitution is named; the ride reaches the floor.\n- `a_centre_cutting_cutter_keeps_its_axial_plunge` - the same audit convicts the centre-cutting path (control: it dives on the axis, unchanged).\n- `an_undrilled_hole_too_tight_for_a_ramp_or_helix_is_refused_by_name`.\n\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 1 step, 0 failed. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --tests -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n**Not exercised.** Verify/post gate on these paths (the generator already substitutes or refuses); stock standing above the hole's mouth (the ladder's top of cut is the hole's `entry_z` - the generic 2D top-of-cut question, not this one); helix transitions other than the planar links.\n\nNo goldens moved, no snapshot PNGs touched.\n\nChangelog: none\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nRefs #1036 (closed as already done by 874507a8 / 515525c4)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
